urname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Zhengyang</forename><surname>Liang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Shitao</forename><surname>Xiao</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Minghao</forename><surname>Qin</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Xi</forename><surname>Yang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Yongping</forename><surname>Xiong</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Bo</forename><surname>Zhang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Keep only edge (f * , v) and remove others 25: end for 26: Initialize mapping dictionary M ← ∅ 27: for (f, v) ∈ E do 28: Add mapping M</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2025\">2025</date>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"volume\">21</biblScope>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"page\" from=\"13691\" to=\"13701\" />\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Let N v = {f j | (f j , v) ∈ E} Proceedings of the Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference f 29: end for 30: return M Prompt of Semantic Memory Synthesis (GPT-4o, Gemini-1.5-Pro</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b62\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">You are provided with the following data: [Video]: 16 frames of a video. (Gemini-1.5-Pro Variant: A video clip in mp4 format</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b63\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">A list of facial features detected in the video</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>each linked to a unique face ID (e.g., &lt;face_1&gt;</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b64\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">A list of speech segments in the video, including start_time, end_time, speaker ID</title>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">&lt;voice_2&gt;), and the corresponding transcribed text</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Video Descriptions]: A description of the video</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b65\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">A list of high-level conclusions that may contain inadequate or incorrect information</title>\n\t\t<idno>Gemini-1.5-Pro Variant:</idno>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Refence conclusions</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b66\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Your Task: Based on the given character features, video content, and reference conclusions, generate a list of high-level, reasoning-based conclusions within the scope of the following category</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b67\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Character-Level Attributes</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b68\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Semantic Memory (the ordered list of high-level thinking conclusions)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b69\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Avoid restating visual facts-focus on identity construction. (c) Interpersonal Relationships &amp; Dynamics -Describe the relationships and interactions between characters: Roles (e.g., host-guest, leader-subordinate)</title>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Emotions or tone (e.g., respect, tension), Power dynamics (e.g., who leads)</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Use the exact format: Equivalence: &lt;face_x&gt;, &lt;voice_y&gt; Include as many confident matches as possible. (b) Character-level Attributes -Infer abstract attributes for each character such as: Name (if explicitly stated Personality (e.g., confident, nervous Role/profession (e.g., host, newcomer), Interests or background (when inferable), istinctive behaviors or traits (e.g., speaks formally, fidgets) Produce concise, high-level reasoning-based conclusions across five categories: (a) Equivalence Identification -Identify which face and voice features refer to the same character Evidence of cooperation, exclusion, conflict, etc. (d) Video-level Plot Understanding -Summarize the scene-level narrative such as: Main event or theme, Narrative arc or sequence (e.g., intro → discussion → reaction Overall tone (e.g., formal, tense Cause-effect or group dynamics. (e) Contextual &amp; General Knowledge -Include general knowledge that can be learned from the video such as: Likely setting or genre (e.g., corporate meeting, game show Cultural/procedural norms Real-world knowledge (e.g., &quot;Alice market is pet-friendly&quot;), Common-sense or format conventions. Strict Requirements (apply to both sections unless noted</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b70\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">If a character has a provided feature ID</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>refer to that character only with the ID (e.g. &lt;face_1&gt;, &lt;voice_2&gt;</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b71\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">If no ID exists, use a short descriptive phrase</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b72\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Keep face/voice IDs consistent throughout</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b73\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Describe only what is grounded in the video or obviously inferable</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b74\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Include natural Time &amp; Location cues and setting hints when inferable</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b75\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Each Episodic Memory line must express one event/detail; split sentences if needed</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b76\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title/>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"j\">Output English only</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b77\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Output a Python list of sentences for each memory type</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n\t\t\t\t</listBibl>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</back>\n\t</text>\n</TEI>\n","pdf_hash":"ec76addce1029afb1c75557f1bea7b1eaa7983e5fb804605c8ee23b03cd8e362","tables":[{"table_id":"tab_0","section_path_id":"1~104","section_ordinal":122,"caption":"Table 8","coordinates":null,"cells":[{"row":0,"column":0,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"Event ID","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":822,"end":830},"digest":"f27cf35f918b1c2373fbac46ab6978f81be160a5962e8078142d559df18391ad"},{"row":0,"column":1,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"Event","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":830,"end":835},"digest":"2fe464f4bf6a377d01fa72064e7b6adc6918e45b7eeace62b8a09ed4d83b50b1"},{"row":0,"column":2,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":835,"end":835},"digest":"5dbad9eed60d7ef498ff00ca6d522d5dcd4cdf962b95572a85b53e5e9504f672"},{"row":1,"column":0,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"1","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":835,"end":836},"digest":"06ad0dc12cc41f53a0f74fe89d9cdfa372f975dc597b8a04bc4ede3ace907e7c"},{"row":1,"column